# Mouseless Linux udev rules (plan §10.6).
#
# /dev/uinput write access is granted to the existing `uinput` group, which
# already contains `kanata-svc`; the daemon joins it. The human desktop user
# needs `mouseless` for the overlay socket, so reusing that group here would
# let the user inject synthetic input — keep the groups separate.
#
# Pointer accuracy is closed-loop in the daemon (bounded REL steps + cursor
# re-query); no libinput acceleration override is used.
# `LIBINPUT_ATTR_POINTER_ACCEL` is not a public libinput knob, so the old
# flat-accel rule was removed.

KERNEL=="uinput", GROUP="uinput", MODE="0660"
